# SpaceWise environment example.
#
# Copy to `.env` only if you are working on an optional feature that needs one.
# Nothing here is required to build, scan, analyse or clean:
#
#   - the application is fully client-side
#   - scanning, analysis and cleanup work with the network disabled
#   - there is no telemetry, no analytics and no activation server
#
# Never commit a real value. Every entry below is a placeholder.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Update feed (optional, release engineering only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The provider is configured in package.json under build.publish. Setting a
# token here is only for a local publish dry run. Never ship one in the app.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional storage summary (implemented; configured inside the app)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The summary is opt-in and needs a licence. Its endpoint and API key are set
# by the person using the application and stored in their own user data
# directory -- which is why there is deliberately no variable for them here.
# They must not be moved into the build: a key shipped in the client is not a
# secret. If the feature is ever extended, it must keep sending the minimum
# metadata and must never upload file contents or full paths by default.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licence issuing (VENDOR SIDE ONLY, never in a distributed build)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Ed25519 private key used to sign licences must never be committed, never
# be placed in the application, and never be exposed to CI for a release build.
# Sign licences on an offline machine and keep the key there.
# SPACEWISE_LICENCE_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/path/to/offline/private-key.pem
